  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to focus on the least probable outcome (minimum probability) of each lottery and prefer the one with the more favorable (higher) value in that outcome. The individual did not refer to the minimum probability outcomes (e.g., 0 Euros in A or 2400 Euros in B at 100%) or compare their values. Instead, their justification was based on the certainty of the outcome in Lottery B. The information considered (certainty) does not align with the information required by the reason (minimum probability outcomes). The justification (preference for certainty) also does not match the rule of the reason (preference based on the value of the least probable outcome). Therefore, the individual did not use the specified decision reason. However, the individual did consider the minimum probability outcome in Lottery A (0 Euros), but only implicitly, as it was not discussed. The absence of any mention of probabilities below 1% or the comparison of minimum-probability outcomes suggests the reason was not applied. The reasoning is based on risk aversion and certainty, not on the specific rule of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
